  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1242 PM CDT Mon Jul 20 2026\n\n*** PROLONGED HOT AND DRY CONDITIONS ***\n\nAs we undergo subsident drying Wed-Thu underneath the upper \nridge, which is progged to be just shy of 600 dm at 500mb, we \nexpect temperatures to rise even further. NBM temperature \nguidance, which is a bit on the cool side of the latest model \nruns, shows highs about 99 to 103 on the Caprock and 103 to 108 in\nthe Rolling Plains. This will support Heat Advisories each day \nfor the Rolling Plains. But we'll also watch to see if temps end \nup a little hotter than forecast up on the Caprock as we may need\nan advisory there as well.\n\nAs it stands now, temperatures are forecast to peak Friday through\nSunday with highs in the Rolling Plains nearing 110, which is the\nexcessive heat warning criteria. There will be little relief at\nnight either, with lows in the middle 70s to near 80. Thus the \nheat risk in the Rolling Plains will build and could become an \nextreme danger, something we'll have to monitor through the \nweekend.\n\nBy Friday, a shortwave will be rounding the ridge through the \nHigh Plains, and is expected to generate some convective activity\nacross nrn New Mexico and along a front/outflow boundary sagging \nsouthward from western KS into the Panhandles. There's a chance \nsome of this activity could reach our northern counties late \nFriday evening or Friday night, and there's also a small potential\nthat greater coverage of shower activity and lingering cloud \ncover could lower highs across portions of the area Saturday, and \nbring a chance of showers and t-storms Saturday, another \npossibility that we'll be watching for.\n\nLate weekend into early next weekend, medium range guidance\nsuggests that the upper-high center will gradually shift westward \nto the 4-corners region. This may allow temperatures to back off \njust a little bit, but it will still remain hot. This could also\nopen the door for some nocturnal convection and/or a weak front \nto enter the picture by late Monday or so, but confidence that \nfar out is very low.",
